# F43 — gt-input-remap overlay for the RSDK Sonic ports. RSDKv4/vB reads
# SDL_GameController, which IS recognized correctly on h700 (probe-confirmed
# isGameController=1, valid mapping), but controls stay dead — an
# RSDK-internal defect this pak cannot fix natively. Fall back to the pak's
# keyboard-synthesis path: gt-input-remap.so (preloaded via
# assets/gt-remap-ports.txt) reads this file and synthesizes SDL key events
# from gamepad presses, matching RSDK's [Keyboard 1] settings.ini scancodes
# (Up=82 Down=81 Left=80 Right=79, A=29(z) B=27(x) X=4(a) Y=22(s),
# Start=40(enter)). Only the `name = key` subset gt-input-remap.c's parser
# accepts is used here (see gt_button_slot/gt_dir_slot/gt_keyname).
#
# back = esc is deliberately KEPT (not repurposed to tab/Select) to preserve
# a quit path — remapping it away locked a user out in a prior session.
back = esc
start = enter
a = z
b = x
x = a
y = s
up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right
